      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "`dumptxoutset` checks `ActiveChain().Contains(*target_index)` under `cs_main` at `blockchain.cpp:3161`, but `CreateRolledBackUTXOSnapshot` pins the tip under a separate lock at `:3296`.\n\nIs it intentional that if the target leaves the active chain between these two points, the operation can still reach `CHECK_NONFATAL(rollback_cache.GetBestBlock() == target->GetBlockHash())` at `:3365`?\n\nI reproduced this on regtest by blocking the first `rollback` call on a FIFO, invalidating the target block, generating 8 new blocks, and then allowing the dump to proceed. Both master and the PR branch hit the check, although the node remains up.\n\nWould it make sense to revalidate the target against the pinned tip immediately after `tip = chainstate.m_chain.Tip()`?\n\n```cpp\nif (tip->GetAncestor(target->nHeight) != target) {\n    throw JSONRPCError(RPC_INVALID_PARAMETER, \"Block is not in main chain\");\n}\n```\n\nWith this check, the same reproduction returns `-8 Block is not in main chain`, and the subsequent `latest` dump succeeds. The relevant tests (`rpc_dumptxoutset.py` and `feature_assumeutxo.py`) also pass.\n\nTested on regtest, head 31000db0ea, Linux aarch64 (Debian 13), GCC 14.2.0, Release.\n",
