      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "> Would it make sense to revalidate the target against the pinned tip immediately after `tip = chainstate.m_chain.Tip()`?\r\n\r\nNot a big problem but it seemed worth addressing. I moved the check there instead of adding a second one, so there is still only one check now and it runs against the pinned tip. This also covers `type=rollback` without an explicit `rollback` option. I like this better because it's cleaner.\r\n\r\nThe one draw-back of this that I ran into: Since the check now runs after the output file is opened, a stale target would leave an empty `.incomplete` file behind. I added 755a45b95fc to remove that file when a dump fails. It also cleans up after the other errors that happen once the file is open, so it doesn't just fix the regression mentioned above but also is a general improvement for another (minor) issue.",
      "user": {
        "login": "fjahr",
        "id": 1322187,
